INSERT INTO feature VALUES('cost-effect','effects','decalf''s cost effect','effect-theories','partial','uncommon','dependent provers','`std.cost` states `Cost.Eff`, decalf''s cost effect homed in the module `Cost`: a charge, and the cost monoid''s unit and sum as value operations, with decalf''s two laws, charging nothing the identity and two charges one charge of their sum, each a rule the path order orients. Its model `Counting` counts in the prelude''s binary naturals, a cost the function that adds it, so its unit is the identity, its sum composition, and it proves both laws by conversion. A scope over `Cost.Eff` names the model that answers it, and a run''s count is at most a bound exactly when `Count.le` holds, so a closed bound is a path to `true` that conversion decides and the kernel replays. A bound below a run''s count is refused `EndpointMismatch`. A model whose charge leaves its continuation as it is reads a run extensionally. A bound over a run that may not end holds at each clock: conversion decides the count of a structural recursion that charges at each clock, a partial run that does not end has no count, and a partial run''s count is never a path endpoint, so only its run reports it. One handler over every thunk that charges and the certificate''s cost delta are owed.','surface-lowering','library/std/src/cost.gandr corpus/ledger/features/cost-effect.gandr corpus/model/effects/cost-clock.gandr corpus/pathological/effects/cost-bound-too-small.gandr corpus/pathological/effects/cost-model.gandr crates/surface-lowering/src/lower/capability/tests.rs crates/surface-lowering-base/src/lower/capability/theory/tests.rs','corpus/ledger/features/cost-effect.gandr','#1106 #3702');
